.TH "CSDLC-RECOVER" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-recover \- preview and execute recovery of one retained native operation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&csdlc recover ISSUE [\-\-repo\-root ROOT] [\-\-json]
\&csdlc recover ISSUE \-\-execute \-\-preview DIGEST
\&csdlc recover ISSUE \-\-disposition DISPOSITION.json \-\-execute \-\-preview DIGEST
\&csdlc recover \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&Semantic issue intent forms are the current operational contract. Direct issue\-writer \-\-request forms are retired and remain available only through \-\-help and \-\-describe for migration discovery. Observation and administrative request forms retain their documented contracts. See docs/csdlc\-v3/INTENT_COMMANDS.md for strict content and effect boundaries.
.PP
\&Preview retained issue journals, pending Finish/FinishWithoutPr, native local transactions or original remote mutations and return preview_digest without token files or mutation. Ordinary issue recovery needs no extra operation input; repository\-scoped creation journal activation requires explicit \-\-disposition selection.
.PP
\&For a creation journal, \-\-disposition contains only schema csdlc.v3.creation_journal_recovery_disposition.v1 and operation_id from the retained semantic operation. Preview with this selection, then repeat it with \-\-execute \-\-preview DIGEST. Authentication binds retained effective authority and checkout head, including any prior authenticated recovery adoption; unadopted changes, corrupt bytes or stale preview fail closed. Only the retained commit is activated; no business effect is replayed. See INTENT_COMMANDS.md for the exact object and follow\-up reconciliation.
.PP
\&Execution requires the exact current preview token. Local recovery holds the native issue lock and compares its current transaction identity. Remote recovery binds the issue snapshot and complete retained native intent bytes, then reconciles the original request without recomputing its operation.
.PP
\&If a proof attempt has no retained outcome, preview reports the required typed abandonment disposition. Explicit abandonment records Failure with Unknown effect truth and never reruns validators; a later explicit proof starts a distinct attempt.
.PP
\&Only the existing remote owner can permit its supported one\-shot authenticated\-absence retry. Merge and unsupported operation retries remain reconciliation\-only. Multiple pending remote operations, or simultaneous local and remote uncertainty, are refused explicitly. With no pending work the result is a no\-op.
.PP
\&A completed semantic publication can retain an unsettled PR update transport. Recover authenticates its exact retained title, body, marker and head, then writes only the transport receipt. Completed semantic history is unchanged. Metadata mismatch, missing target or unavailable readback remains blocked: legacy update intents have no authenticated prior metadata, so these observations cannot safely authorize redispatch. The original retry budget and supported authenticated absence routes remain unchanged.
.PP
\&Preserve native journals, intents and receipts. A changed token or request is not permission to bypass a guard. Source implementation requires focused installed proof and does not imply active binary replacement.
.PP
\&For a pending RecordMerge that must be replaced after integration, an explicit csdlc.v3.semantic_merge_retirement_disposition.v1 selects action retire_never_dispatched_merge, exact operation_id and nonempty rationale. Preview with \-\-disposition, then execute the same disposition with \-\-execute \-\-preview DIGEST. Retirement requires authenticated open/unmerged PR identity and no dispatch\-prestate, input, response, reconciliation or receipt object under the PR lock. Any uncertainty refuses retirement. A durable fence precedes semantic Failure/NotPerformed; original intent and target remain immutable. Fresh successor proof/review/publication/ready and an append\-only single\-successor guard are required. Retired operations never dispatch again. See INTENT_COMMANDS.md for the object and continuation.
.PP
\&The generated wrapper emitted by \-\-emit\-request can be passed directly to \-\-intent\-request; the inner request is also accepted.
.SH OUTPUT
\&Machine JSON uses the common command\-result envelope. Interpret status, authority, effects and findings independently. An emitted request is a snapshot, not execution. Foreign\-platform snapshot rejection is not non\-Unix execution proof.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&csdlc(1), csdlc\-requests(1), csdlc\-workflow(1), docs/csdlc\-v3/INTENT_COMMANDS.md.
.SH OPTIONS
\&Supported candidate intent options: \-\-disposition, \-\-emit\-request, \-\-execute, \-\-help, \-\-intent\-request, \-\-json, \-\-preview, \-\-repo\-root, \-h. Positional ISSUE is positive; \-\-help and \-h are standalone discovery. Unsupported combinations fail closed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\&csdlc recover ISSUE [\-\-repo\-root ROOT] [\-\-json]
\&csdlc recover ISSUE \-\-execute \-\-preview DIGEST
\&csdlc recover ISSUE \-\-disposition DISPOSITION.json \-\-execute \-\-preview DIGEST
\&csdlc recover \-\-intent\-request REQUEST.json
.fi
.PP
\&These forms require a supporting selected candidate; they do not upgrade the active binary or authorize activation.
